  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Starting from Plage de Cabasson, this easy trail alternates between beaches and rocky stretches, with a stunning view of the Fort de Brégançon, secret coves and fragrant pine woods all along the route.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Dogs are allowed on a leash for the whole route (source: ville-bormes.fr and the Bormes tourist office), but the swimming rule differs depending on the exact beach: banned all year at l'Estagnol, banned from March to November at Cabasson (allowed the rest of the year), and allowed all year at Brégançon. Closed shoes are recommended, as the trail alternates between beaches and rocky areas. The walk is suitable for children. The Plage de Cabasson car park is paid from April to October (it's a private car park, rates vary by source between €11 and €13/day), but free in winter.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: to avoid the paid car park, you can start from La Londe-les-Maures (+9 km) — a simple trick worth the detour out of season.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Fort de Brégançon dominates the landscape, and Bormes-les-Mimosas is just a few minutes away to extend the walk.</p>
